  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Here are the savings targets for every big birthday, from twenty-five to fifty. See which ones you hit.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "bank",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "clock"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Saved by",
            "25, 30, 40, 50?"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The rule of thumb scales with your salary. Half by twenty-five, one time by thirty, three by forty, six by fifty.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "Multiples of salary",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "25",
              "name": "Age 25",
              "value": "0.5×",
              "note": "half a salary",
              "color": "#5c544c",
              "bar": 0.15
            },
            {
              "rank": "30",
              "name": "Age 30",
              "value": "1×",
              "note": "one salary",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.3
            },
            {
              "rank": "40",
              "name": "Age 40",
              "value": "3×",
              "note": "three salaries",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.6
            },
            {
              "rank": "50",
              "name": "Age 50",
              "value": "6×",
              "note": "six salaries",
              "color": "#c0392b",
              "bar": 1.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The targets rise steeply because compounding is doing the heavy lifting.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-compound",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · compound interest"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The single easiest way to hit them is free money from your employer's match.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "free money",
          "label": "the employer match",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "An employer match tops up your own contributions, for free.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-match",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · employer matching"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Five hundred dollars a month from twenty-five to sixty-five can grow to about a million.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "$1M",
          "label": "$500/mo from 25 to 65",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Most people reach it inside a tax-advantaged 401(k).",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-401k",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · 401(k)"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The jump from three times to six times your salary is where it gets serious.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "3× to 6×",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Steady monthly investing, dollar cost averaging, is how most people get there.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-dca",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · dollar cost averaging"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
